Must-do (client-architecture.md §11):

- Initial JS: raised from 190 KB to 192 KB gzipped (measured 190.0 KB when the app handoff
  landed). The screens are not code-split — only the heavy libraries are — so every feature
  ratchets the initial bundle. Split the screens so the first paint stops paying for the
  terminal and the file manager, then bring the budget back down.

- L4 (daemon): an `input` refusal (`busy`, `inputTooLarge`) names no request, so the client cannot
  report which typed characters were refused. Paste refusals now carry their request id; the
  terminal's short input batch remains necessary until input has its own result contract.
- Phone dock (P3a): landscape and keyboard-up behaviour need the real-iPhone checklist
  (`.meridian/work/tether-mvp/g3-iphone-checklist.md`).
- W5 (device): the native keyboard toggle (`focus terminal`/`hidden`), `keyboardInset`, rotation,
  `select` and the long-press callout were built but not exercised: the Simulator takes no touch
  or key input from the agent shell. They are on `ios-shell.md`'s Device checklist and the
  checklist (18 to 29).
